WEBVTT

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:18.530
It was just another summer day.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:27.120
Hey there, cutie. You alone?

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:29.160
Maki-chan?

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:31.620
Hey, long time no see.

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:33.950
What's up? Waiting for someone?

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:36.160
No, Aya-chan is on a trip,

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:39.620
and Midori-chan is busy making her game.

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:43.390
Huh? Miki-chan, are those two
the only friends you have?

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:47.450
Right, then! You can hang out with me today.

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:48.620
Huh?

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:51.850
Maki-chan! Too fast!

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:53.700
Say what?

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:55.830
Slow down!

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:58.080
I know, it feels good, right?

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:00.910
I'm going faster, hold on tight!

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:01.740
What?!

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:46.830
Okay, we're here.

00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:53.040
Wait, were you that scared?

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:56.200
Jeez, if you told me,
I would have slowed down.

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:58.200
I-I did tell you...

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:00.120
Oh, well.

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:04.910
Come on, over here.

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:11.000
Wow, so cold!

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:15.500
What are you waiting for?
Get in here! It feels good.

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:16.790
Okay.

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:23.250
You're right, it does feel good.

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:28.290
Whoa, fish!

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:31.330
Do you think I can grab them with my hands?

00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:32.870
Wait! Hey!

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:35.480
Maki-chan, you might
want to slow down a bit...

00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:39.660
Maki-chan!

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:42.910
Oh, I asked for that one...

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:49.200
Hey, who are you laughing at?

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:50.410
There!

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:56.200
There! That feels good, doesn't it?

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:57.830
Maki-chan?!

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:03.910
We don't even have a change of clothes...

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:09.000
Don't worry so much. This'll dry up super quick.

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:17.160
The wind sure does feel good!

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:25.790
That game we played at Hana's,
that was really fun, wasn't it?

00:04:25.790 --> 00:04:27.540
Oh, <i>Incan Gold?</i>

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:28.950
Yeah, that one.

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:32.120
Board games are nice.

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:37.700
Once you become an adult, you rarely have
the chance to play with others like that.

00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:41.750
Also, that's what got us to get close.

00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:44.750
Oh, I remember. Wait one sec.

00:04:46.250 --> 00:04:47.080
Here.

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:49.540
What's this? Dice?

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:53.950
It's <i>Monjiro</i>. I bought it the
other day, and left it in my bag.

00:04:53.950 --> 00:04:58.370
I haven't played it yet, but it says
you can play many games with these.

00:04:58.370 --> 00:04:59.790
Is that so?

00:04:59.790 --> 00:05:01.120
Let me see.

00:05:03.160 --> 00:05:06.160
I see, looks interesting.

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:09.500
Right then, let's try one out.

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:11.660
How about this "<i>Monjiro</i> Showdown"?

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:12.750
Okay.

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:17.120
First we take these kana dice
and take half each.

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:20.330
We line them up to make
insults to hurl at each other.

00:05:20.330 --> 00:05:21.160
Huh?!

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:22.200
Here I go!

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:23.700
Hey, Maki-chan...

00:05:24.200 --> 00:05:25.420
How 'bout this?

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:29.760
Next is...

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:36.680
Don't you have any? Get me back! Come on.

00:05:41.950 --> 00:05:45.660
Delinquent?! That's barely an insult!

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:47.860
You suck at insults, Miki-chan!

00:05:51.070 --> 00:05:53.950
Six characters? Not bad.

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:56.620
In that case, how's this?

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:03.040
Hah, no effect!

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:03.960
There!

00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:05.870
A dog?!

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:09.210
Too weak!

00:06:09.210 --> 00:06:10.000
There!

00:06:11.540 --> 00:06:12.920
Why is she so...

00:06:15.250 --> 00:06:16.620
No damage!

00:06:17.870 --> 00:06:21.350
Why is she enjoying hurling insults so much?!

00:06:23.870 --> 00:06:26.790
Miki-chan, you're really bad
at insulting people.

00:06:26.790 --> 00:06:29.440
Have you ever been in
a shouting match before?

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:34.910
By the way, Miki-chan, how does this end?

00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:35.860
Huh?

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:39.330
It doesn't say...

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:43.290
Oh, well. Maybe you should
surrender. Just say I won.

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:45.450
N-No! I refuse!

00:06:45.450 --> 00:06:48.210
Yes, of course. You're actually quite...

00:06:50.790 --> 00:06:52.590
That's not...

00:06:54.910 --> 00:06:55.840
Maki-chan...

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:00.510
"Thank you"?

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:04.410
What's this? Did you misspell
"I'm going to kick your butt"?

00:07:04.410 --> 00:07:09.700
No, I've been wanting to
thank you properly for a while.

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:15.660
You might not remember,
but a long time ago, you saved me.

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:17.250
Back when I was in grade school.

00:07:17.250 --> 00:07:21.450
At the shrine. The stuffed bear.

00:07:21.450 --> 00:07:25.790
So it really was you back then.

00:07:25.790 --> 00:07:29.040
I remember you were bullied there often.

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:29.910
Yes.

00:07:29.910 --> 00:07:33.330
Oh, but after you saved me, they stopped.

00:07:33.330 --> 00:07:35.830
So annoying.

00:07:35.830 --> 00:07:37.000
Maki-chan?

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:40.950
My dad was a real train wreck of a person.

00:07:40.950 --> 00:07:43.330
He loved gambling and was always drunk.

00:07:43.330 --> 00:07:47.830
He'd come home wasted
and hit my mom or us kids.

00:07:47.830 --> 00:07:49.950
I got hit a lot, too.

00:07:49.950 --> 00:07:56.120
My parents got divorced, and my mom
moved with us kids out to Kyoto.

00:07:57.120 --> 00:08:00.830
But those memories will never go away.

00:08:02.200 --> 00:08:06.080
Whenever I see an idiot pick on
someone who can't fight back,

00:08:06.080 --> 00:08:10.370
it reminds me of my garbage dad
and I can't stop myself.

00:08:10.370 --> 00:08:12.000
Maki-chan...

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:15.450
So it's really not something
you should thank me for.

00:08:15.450 --> 00:08:21.580
I wasn't trying to save you.
I just wanted to vent.

00:08:21.580 --> 00:08:26.910
Back then, whenever I saw
someone like that, I beat them up.

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:32.620
And that's how I earned
the name "Mad Dog Kyoko."

00:08:33.790 --> 00:08:36.500
Maki-chan... She's so...

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:40.990
Maki-chan, how are you able to smile like that?

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:42.250
Huh?

00:08:42.250 --> 00:08:45.200
How can I become strong like that?

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:48.910
I know that I'm a weakling.

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:53.750
I feel so ashamed that I'm
like this, and I want to change.

00:08:53.750 --> 00:08:58.830
But I can't. I don't have the courage,
I'm afraid of so many things,

00:08:58.830 --> 00:09:01.620
and I'm always running from things.

00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:04.750
I want to be strong like you!

00:09:04.750 --> 00:09:07.890
What are you talking about? Don't bother.

00:09:11.410 --> 00:09:13.870
Well, um, you know.

00:09:13.870 --> 00:09:17.290
I get carried away too easily. It's who I am.

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:18.790
So, like, um...

00:09:18.790 --> 00:09:20.870
...forgive me!

00:09:20.870 --> 00:09:23.330
You don't insult people at all because
you're a compassionate person

00:09:23.330 --> 00:09:27.250
who can understand what it feels
like to have those things said to you.

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:29.950
You're a much better person than I am, by a lot.

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:37.620
Hey, Miki-chan.

00:09:39.330 --> 00:09:45.540
You said you're always
running away. Are you sure?

00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:50.250
At least, when we played at Hana's,
you didn't run from me, you faced me.

00:09:50.250 --> 00:09:53.790
Also, compared to back then,
you're smiling much more.

00:09:55.040 --> 00:09:56.910
Yes.

00:09:56.910 --> 00:10:01.160
I'm having a lot of fun every day.

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:04.080
Hey, Maki-chan. Want to try a different game?

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:05.030
A different game?

00:10:06.950 --> 00:10:08.120
Love-love?

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:09.580
We complement each other.

00:10:09.580 --> 00:10:12.000
No way! That's gross.

00:10:12.580 --> 00:10:13.580
There.

00:10:13.580 --> 00:10:16.790
Strong? Is that a compliment?

00:10:16.790 --> 00:10:18.540
Huh? Well, how about...

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:23.720
...this?

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:27.250
You know, Miki-chan,
you can't just say random stuff.

00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:32.250
It's not! When you were drying your hair,
I was surprised by how pretty you were!

00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:34.870
What are you talking about?!

00:10:34.870 --> 00:10:36.450
She's blushing.

00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:38.910
Maki-chan!

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:41.000
What?!

00:10:44.950 --> 00:10:48.620
Stop! Stop! This is a lot harder for me!

00:10:48.620 --> 00:10:49.660
Look, got another one!

00:10:51.870 --> 00:10:54.250
This girl...

00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:57.370
She might have a hidden sadistic side...

00:10:57.540 --> 00:10:58.380
There!

00:10:59.540 --> 00:11:02.950
And that's how my summer break ended.

00:11:05.870 --> 00:11:08.160
The next trimester began.

00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:12.620
We started off by planning the
school festival coming up in autumn.

00:11:12.620 --> 00:11:16.080
We decided to pitch the idea
of doing a board game café,

00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:19.790
in addition to what our class
was already planning, but...

00:11:21.290 --> 00:11:22.320
Denied.

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:30.370
Huh?! What?!

00:11:30.370 --> 00:11:32.660
Just straight-up denied?!

00:11:32.660 --> 00:11:33.910
Wait, are you...

00:11:33.910 --> 00:11:38.420
...holding a grudge against us, because
Midori-chan turned you down the other day?

00:11:39.200 --> 00:11:42.920
You can think whatever you like,
but no means no.

00:11:44.250 --> 00:11:46.220
Understood. Excuse us.

00:11:47.830 --> 00:11:49.660
What, Midori-chan?

00:11:49.660 --> 00:11:50.720
Excuse me.

00:11:55.660 --> 00:11:59.120
Is she allowed to do that? It's abuse of power!

00:11:59.120 --> 00:12:02.540
There's nothing we can do. Let's give up.

00:12:02.540 --> 00:12:05.580
But is that really the whole story...?

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:12.450
Is something wrong, Miki?

00:12:17.450 --> 00:12:22.700
Board games are fun. I know, I tried.

00:12:22.700 --> 00:12:29.830
But I can't rely on Midori any longer.
I have to make the best school festival ever.

00:12:29.830 --> 00:12:31.120
And...

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:34.370
I'm going to get Senpai to think highly of me!

00:12:34.370 --> 00:12:36.080
Wassup?

00:12:36.080 --> 00:12:38.120
I'm back, guys!

00:12:38.120 --> 00:12:40.000
Senpai?!

00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:42.000
Huh, it's just you here, Shibusawa?

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:44.750
You could have let us know if you were coming!

00:12:44.750 --> 00:12:47.000
I'm getting the others!

00:12:48.290 --> 00:12:49.530
Hmm?

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:55.410
Seems like they put a lot of thought into this.
This is going to be a fun festival.

00:12:55.410 --> 00:12:58.620
Shibusawa is really working hard.

00:13:00.080 --> 00:13:00.830
Hmm?

00:13:02.660 --> 00:13:07.460
Board game café, planned by... Ono Midori?

00:13:07.910 --> 00:13:09.210
A first-year?

00:13:10.500 --> 00:13:12.910
This isn't fair!

00:13:12.910 --> 00:13:15.120
Aya-chan, are you still mad?

00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:16.580
I mean, come on!

00:13:16.580 --> 00:13:21.370
This was the opportunity to let everyone
learn about Midori-chan's dream!

00:13:21.370 --> 00:13:25.580
It's fine. I don't need
everyone to know about it.

00:13:25.580 --> 00:13:27.040
Welcome!

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:33.540
This person... I saw him
in the hallway earlier...

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:35.750
Our school uniform...

00:13:35.750 --> 00:13:39.250
I see. These three must be the applicants.

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:42.870
Are you looking for a game in particular?

00:13:42.870 --> 00:13:44.830
Huh? Oh, no, um...

00:13:44.830 --> 00:13:48.000
It's my first time here,
and I don't know anything.

00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:51.040
This is a shop selling
games of some sort, right?

00:13:51.040 --> 00:13:53.830
Yes, this is a shop specializing in board games.

00:13:53.830 --> 00:13:56.250
Board games! Yes, that.

00:13:56.250 --> 00:14:00.200
Would you like to try one out?

00:14:00.200 --> 00:14:02.450
Oh, is that a thing you can do here?

00:14:02.450 --> 00:14:07.330
Yes, the best way to learn about
board games is to try playing one.

00:14:07.330 --> 00:14:10.620
In that case, sure! But...

00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:13.000
That's a huge selection of games.

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:16.410
There are many types of board games.

00:14:16.410 --> 00:14:21.540
If there is a certain type of game you like,
I can find something for you.

00:14:21.540 --> 00:14:24.700
Hmm, let's see...

00:14:24.700 --> 00:14:26.540
A festival...

00:14:26.540 --> 00:14:30.870
Something where we all can get
excited and laugh together, like a festival.

00:14:30.870 --> 00:14:33.040
A festival?

00:14:33.040 --> 00:14:35.750
Do you have anything like that?

00:14:35.750 --> 00:14:38.870
Understood, one moment please.

00:14:40.160 --> 00:14:43.350
<i>THE ISLAND</i> by Julian Courtland-Smith.

00:14:43.660 --> 00:14:46.290
In this game, the island of Atlantis is sinking,

00:14:46.290 --> 00:14:49.120
and your goal is to lead your
exploration party to safety.

00:14:49.120 --> 00:14:50.790
I see. Go on.

00:14:50.790 --> 00:14:56.040
First, you lay out these hexagonal
land tiles to create the island.

00:14:56.040 --> 00:15:00.040
On spaces where you see the dragon icon,
place this Sea Serpent piece.

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:06.080
Each player has ten people pieces,
each with a value of one to six on the bottom.

00:15:06.080 --> 00:15:07.330
I see them!

00:15:07.330 --> 00:15:11.290
This number is added to your score
if the person escapes to safety.

00:15:11.290 --> 00:15:17.500
The island has plains, forests, and
mountain tiles, sinking in that order.

00:15:17.500 --> 00:15:21.580
So placing your pieces on
higher ground is generally safer.

00:15:21.580 --> 00:15:25.410
So let's take turns to
place pieces on the island.

00:15:25.410 --> 00:15:27.040
Okay!

00:15:29.620 --> 00:15:31.660
Wow! This is cool!

00:15:31.660 --> 00:15:33.870
This is impressive!

00:15:33.870 --> 00:15:36.120
Now I will explain how to play the game.

00:15:36.120 --> 00:15:39.080
There are three different things
you can do during your turn.

00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:42.160
First, moving pieces and boats.

00:15:42.160 --> 00:15:44.620
You can move your piece,
a boat containing your piece,

00:15:44.620 --> 00:15:48.700
or an empty boat by up to three spaces total.

00:15:48.700 --> 00:15:53.830
However, a piece that fell in
the ocean can only move one space.

00:15:53.830 --> 00:15:59.620
So for the most part, you want to put
your pieces on a boat to head to the beach.

00:16:00.700 --> 00:16:05.540
Once a piece reaches the beach,
it escapes to safety.

00:16:05.540 --> 00:16:07.200
I see.

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:10.500
Where have I seen this person before?

00:16:10.500 --> 00:16:15.410
When you're done moving your pieces,
you then remove a land tile.

00:16:15.410 --> 00:16:22.080
Plains tiles go first. When you run out
of plains, remove forests, then mountains.

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:25.200
Wait, so if a piece was on that tile...

00:16:25.200 --> 00:16:28.250
It immediately falls into the ocean.

00:16:28.250 --> 00:16:30.750
I have a bad feeling about this...

00:16:30.750 --> 00:16:35.540
Behind each land tile is an image
with either a green or red border.

00:16:35.540 --> 00:16:38.250
Red ones are items, and green ones are events.

00:16:38.250 --> 00:16:42.450
Don't show others if it's an item,
and keep it to yourself for later use.

00:16:42.450 --> 00:16:46.700
You can use an item at the beginning
of your future turns before moving pieces.

00:16:46.700 --> 00:16:47.910
I remember now!

00:16:49.620 --> 00:16:52.870
He's the student council
chairperson from our school!

00:16:52.870 --> 00:16:57.290
Finally, after removing the land tile,
roll this monster die.

00:16:57.290 --> 00:17:01.410
You will move either a Shark,
Whale, or Sea Serpent.

00:17:01.410 --> 00:17:05.410
So if you're removing
the land and adding monsters...

00:17:05.410 --> 00:17:11.700
Yes. As the game goes on, the island
gets smaller and the sea more dangerous.

00:17:11.700 --> 00:17:15.000
Sounds like fun! Let's try it out!

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:20.870
But what is the chairperson doing here?
Scouting the board game café?

00:17:20.870 --> 00:17:23.790
But the café idea was
denied by the vice-chair...

00:17:23.790 --> 00:17:26.040
What's wrong, Miki-chan? Let's play.

00:17:26.040 --> 00:17:29.040
Oh, yeah, I'm fine. Let's play.

00:17:29.040 --> 00:17:34.500
I'll start. One, two, three.
I'll put them in the boat.

00:17:34.500 --> 00:17:35.830
I'll take this land.

00:17:35.830 --> 00:17:38.190
Wait, Midori-chan?! That's mine!

00:17:38.540 --> 00:17:43.580
And on the back is...
Oh, an event. Shark attack.

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:47.580
Since a Shark appeared on
this tile, this piece is dead.

00:17:47.580 --> 00:17:51.330
What?! I lost a man at the beginning!

00:17:51.330 --> 00:17:53.580
I told you, the plains are dangerous!

00:17:53.580 --> 00:17:56.080
No punches pulled, even between friends?

00:17:56.080 --> 00:17:58.410
There is no value in restraint
when it comes to games.

00:17:58.410 --> 00:18:02.500
Especially in this game, <i>THE ISLAND</i>,
the players control the monsters, too.

00:18:02.500 --> 00:18:04.700
If you're too gentle,
it won't be a fun festival.

00:18:04.700 --> 00:18:07.580
All right, then I'll go all in as well.

00:18:07.580 --> 00:18:10.370
Yes, that's the right way.

00:18:10.370 --> 00:18:11.540
Shark!

00:18:11.540 --> 00:18:12.910
Whale!

00:18:12.910 --> 00:18:15.250
Another Shark?

00:18:15.250 --> 00:18:18.290
Before we know it,
the sea is full of Sharks and Whales...

00:18:18.290 --> 00:18:20.660
Looks like this party is getting hotter!

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:25.450
I've got my people in the boat, but
the beach is defended by the Sea Serpent...

00:18:25.450 --> 00:18:29.160
If I approach unprepared,
the monster will get me before I land.

00:18:29.160 --> 00:18:32.370
In that case, I'll take a risk
and jump into the ocean!

00:18:32.370 --> 00:18:37.450
Wait, are you sure?! If you're in the sea,
you can only move one space!

00:18:37.450 --> 00:18:39.290
It's fine!

00:18:39.290 --> 00:18:42.450
I see. You must have drawn the Dolphin item!

00:18:42.450 --> 00:18:43.410
Dolphin?

00:18:43.410 --> 00:18:47.080
The Dolphin can carry a
swimming person three tiles away.

00:18:47.080 --> 00:18:49.790
However, it doesn't work
if the person is on a boat.

00:18:49.790 --> 00:18:51.910
Yep, that's right.

00:18:51.910 --> 00:18:57.250
If I use the Dolphin in my next movement
phase, I can get at least one man to safety.

00:18:57.250 --> 00:18:59.370
Would it be that easy?

00:18:59.370 --> 00:19:00.500
Huh?

00:19:00.500 --> 00:19:02.040
Shark Warp.

00:19:02.040 --> 00:19:06.790
I can move the Shark to any open ocean tile.

00:19:06.790 --> 00:19:09.580
I'll move it next to this Sea Serpent.

00:19:09.580 --> 00:19:10.410
What?!

00:19:10.410 --> 00:19:11.830
You devil.

00:19:11.830 --> 00:19:13.660
Now, rolling the die...

00:19:14.910 --> 00:19:16.040
Shark?!

00:19:16.040 --> 00:19:17.120
What?!

00:19:17.120 --> 00:19:19.330
Oh, no, it really came!

00:19:19.330 --> 00:19:21.040
Dinner time.

00:19:22.370 --> 00:19:25.200
My six point squad leader...

00:19:25.200 --> 00:19:30.370
You can't let your guard down just
because there are no monsters nearby.

00:19:30.370 --> 00:19:36.290
No easy mode, even for a first-time
customer? I like your attitude!

00:19:36.290 --> 00:19:40.120
I won't lose this battle, no matter what!

00:19:42.620 --> 00:19:44.580
This is terrible...

00:19:44.580 --> 00:19:46.830
Only the mountain tiles remain now.

00:19:46.830 --> 00:19:50.580
One of the mountain tiles has
a volcano on the other side.

00:19:50.580 --> 00:19:55.080
The moment that one is turned over,
all non-safe explorers are killed.

00:19:55.080 --> 00:19:57.370
That's the end of the game.

00:19:57.370 --> 00:20:00.290
I've only rescued three people so far!

00:20:00.290 --> 00:20:05.410
Me, too... This is harder than I expected.

00:20:05.410 --> 00:20:06.660
Another ocean dive?!

00:20:06.660 --> 00:20:10.950
One volcano and it's over, right?
Then now is the time to take a risk!

00:20:10.950 --> 00:20:14.620
Okay, me, too! One, two, three!

00:20:14.620 --> 00:20:17.750
Are you sure? If someone rolls
a Sea Serpent, you're doomed!

00:20:17.750 --> 00:20:20.000
I know! Now is the time to go big!

00:20:20.000 --> 00:20:23.370
Good! I like your courage!

00:20:23.370 --> 00:20:28.450
Only those who can take risks at times
like these can get luck on their side!

00:20:28.450 --> 00:20:32.160
Yeah! Let's survive together, brother!

00:20:33.410 --> 00:20:34.580
Oh...

00:20:35.790 --> 00:20:38.790
Um... this...

00:20:38.790 --> 00:20:40.410
Volcano...

00:20:44.950 --> 00:20:47.750
And that's the end of the game.

00:20:49.200 --> 00:20:51.290
I'm in last place...

00:20:51.290 --> 00:20:53.040
Me, too...

00:20:54.790 --> 00:20:56.370
M-Midori-chan...

00:20:56.370 --> 00:20:59.000
Was I too hard on him...?

00:21:01.290 --> 00:21:03.040
You got me!

00:21:03.040 --> 00:21:06.540
We laughed, yelled,
and ended with some fireworks.

00:21:06.540 --> 00:21:09.660
This truly is a festival!

00:21:09.660 --> 00:21:10.750
Wait, so...

00:21:10.750 --> 00:21:12.200
Did you like it?

00:21:12.200 --> 00:21:14.120
Yeah, I had fun!

00:21:14.120 --> 00:21:16.620
Hundred percent!

00:21:16.620 --> 00:21:20.910
They're truly impressive, these board games.

00:21:20.910 --> 00:21:25.370
Yes, they are, Mr. Chairperson.

00:21:25.370 --> 00:21:27.540
Midori-chan, you noticed.

00:21:27.540 --> 00:21:30.080
Huh? What? What's this?

00:21:30.080 --> 00:21:32.080
Oh, you knew?

00:21:32.080 --> 00:21:35.290
Of course. I'm a student at the same school.

00:21:35.290 --> 00:21:37.450
Are there others like this?

00:21:37.450 --> 00:21:42.200
Yes. There are countless
other fun games to discover.

00:21:42.200 --> 00:21:44.160
That's really wild.

00:21:44.160 --> 00:21:47.080
This year's school festival is going to be fun!

00:21:48.500 --> 00:21:53.620
The next day, the board game café
idea denial by the vice-chair

00:21:53.620 --> 00:21:56.950
was overturned by the chairperson,
so the project was officially approved.

00:21:57.410 --> 00:22:01.330
You three, do your best to
make this a great school festival!

00:22:01.330 --> 00:22:02.870
Show me what you've got!

00:22:02.870 --> 00:22:03.750
Yes!

00:22:03.750 --> 00:22:04.960
You can count on us!

00:23:37.500 --> 00:23:42.260
Hey, guys! I went to a
board game café near school.

00:23:42.660 --> 00:23:46.310
There was a super cute girl there!
